# An apt archive is verified byte for byte: Release lists the checksums of
# Packages, and InRelease carries a signature over exactly those bytes. A
# line-ending conversion anywhere in the chain - on checkout, on a colleague's
# machine with core.autocrlf=true, in CI on Windows - turns a valid archive
# into one that apt reports as corrupt, with a hash mismatch that looks like a
# mirror problem rather than a git setting.
#
# So: git treats nothing here as text.
* -text
